Package: tscop
Type: Package
Title: Time Series Copula Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Alexander J.", "McNeil",
      email = "alexanderjmcneil@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Tools for the analysis of time series using copula models, built
    on the udp package: Gaussian ARMA and AR-factor copula processes, stationary
    d-vine copula processes parameterised through the Kendall partial
    autocorrelation function (Bladt and McNeil (2022)
    <doi:10.1515/demo-2022-0105>; Bladt, Dias, Han and McNeil (2026)
    <doi:10.1002/cjs.70033>), and v-transform models for volatile time series:
    process-level v-transforms of Gaussian (McNeil (2021)
    <doi:10.3390/risks9010014>) and non-Gaussian d-vine base processes (Bladt
    and McNeil (2022) <doi:10.1016/j.ecosta.2021.07.004>), and
    inverse-v-transformed pair copulas for stochastic volatility (Dias, Han
    and McNeil (2027) <doi:10.1016/j.jmva.2026.105695>), and parametric marginal distributions (Gaussian,
    Laplace, Student t, skew t, Johnson SU, generalised hyperbolic and its special
    cases) with automatic selection, and empirical margins for the semiparametric
    approach. Under development.
